      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i keep getting a run-time error '1004': application-defined or object-defined error when i try to run this macro for our monthly reconciliation. it works sometimes but then it just crashes. can u see what's wrong?\n\nsub MonthlyRecon()\n    Dim ws As Worksheet\n    Dim lastRow As Long\n    Set ws = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Reconciliation\")\n    \n    lastRow = ws.Cells(ws.Rows.Count, \"A\").End(xlUp).Row\n    \n    For i = 2 To lastRow\n        If ws.Range(\"B\" & i).Value > 1000 Then\n            ws.Range(\"C\" & i).Value = ws.Range(\"B\" & i).Value * 0.05\n        End If\n    Next i\n    \n    ws.Range(\"C1\").Value = \"Tax Calculation\"\nend sub",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A runtime error '1004' during a reconciliation macro, especially when it's intermittent, is often caused by a reference issue or trying to write to a protected cell. It's less likely to be the logic itself, but rather the environment it's running in. You should check if the \"Reconciliation\" sheet is protected, as that can cause the macro to throw a 1004 error when trying to write to column C. If it is protected, you'll need to unprotect it before the loop runs.",
